    <briefdescription>
<para>Arena (bump-pointer) allocator for analytics hot paths. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Implements std::pmr::memory_resource so that any std::pmr container (unordered_map, string, vector, …) can draw memory directly from this arena rather than the global heap.</para>
<para>Keeps one large contiguous primary block (default 64 MiB). When that block is exhausted, overflow slabs are appended. <ref refid="classthemis_1_1analytics_1_1detail_1_1_analytics_memory_pool_1a31168a94e31101352dd3018917ba48de" kindref="member">reset()</ref> rewinds the cursor to 0 and releases overflow slabs — the primary block is retained so steady-state allocations never touch the global heap. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
